---
/**
 * The three iOS facts that decide whether an automatic destination appears to
 * work, repeated on every destination page.
 *
 * Repeating this is deliberate. Someone setting up MQTT reads the MQTT page
 * and nothing else, and "your export did not run" is the most common
 * disappointment in this category of app. A link they will not follow is not
 * an explanation.
 */
import Callout from './Callout.astro';
---

<Callout kind="warn" title="Three things iOS decides, not Hozz">
  <ul>
    <li>
      <strong>Health cannot be read while the phone is locked.</strong> The database is encrypted
      until first unlock. If iOS wakes Hozz on a locked phone, the pass waits rather than
      reporting a delivery it did not make.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>iOS chooses when a background app runs.</strong> A cadence is a request. Most Health
      types are capped at hourly delivery by HealthKit regardless of what is asked for.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Force-quitting Hozz stops background launches</strong> until you open the app again.
      That is an iOS rule that applies to every app, and there is no way around it.
    </li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    <a href="/docs/background-sync/">Background sync, explained honestly</a> covers what Hozz does
    about each of these.
  </p>
</Callout>
